   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Synthwave\n\nA retro neon horizon with a scrolling perspective grid, a rising striped sun and mountain ranges that slide in. The grid keeps scrolling for as long as the clip lasts.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene needs an 80s retro backdrop: a music drop, a gaming or nostalgia beat, a late-night product teaser.\n- Titles or a logo should sit over a moving background that loops for as long as the beat lasts.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The camera should fly forward through space into the next scene: use hyperspace.\n- The backdrop should be a calm landscape that trucks sideways in layers: use parallax-depth.\n\nVariables:\n- sky_top (color): Sky top, default \"#08080B\"\n- sky_horizon (color): Sky horizon, default \"#3B0C10\"\n- sun_top (color): Sun top, default \"#FFC46B\"\n- sun_bottom (color): Sun bottom, default \"#E5322D\"\n- grid_color (color): Grid, default \"#E5322D\"\n- floor_color (color): Floor, default \"#0A0A0C\"\n- mountains_back (color): Back mountains, default \"#2A0A0E\"\n- mountains_front (color): Front mountains, default \"#111111\"\n- grid_speed (number, 0-8): Grid speed, default 2\n- horizon (number, 0.3-0.8): Horizon, default 0.6\n- sun_stripes (boolean): Sun stripes, default true\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
